# {{name}}

{{summary}} Built on [operonx](https://pypi.org/project/operonx/).

`src/textstats/` is the feature: `ops.py` holds the logic, `graph.py` wires
it between the http door's `ingress()` and `egress()`. `app/main.py`
declares the `stats` service that runs it.

## Run

```bash
{{setup}}
{{run}}pytest                 # the tests, offline; the service is called in-process
```

## Serve

```bash
{{run}}operonx serve --list   # what would listen, and where
{{run}}operonx serve          # POST /stats on :8000 (PORT overrides)
curl -s localhost:8000/stats -d '{"text": "hello operonx"}'
```

## Grow it

A new feature is a new folder under `src/` with its own `graph.py` and
`ops.py`, and one more `Service` (or `Job`) in `app/main.py`. Read
`AGENTS.md` and `.operonx/guide/README.md` first.
